{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
  "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I address a preliminary inquiry that I have? Are we reviewing here the issuance of the injunction by the trial court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our principal submission is that Congress's designation in Schedule 1 is sufficient unto itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I -- may I ask you one question about the procedural posture of this case? This is an appeal from a preliminary injunction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is an appeal from a preliminary injunction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what do you -- here's the problem that I have, particularly at the stage of the preliminary injunction, with that argument. The -- they're -- the Convention also includes that provision that its terms will be defined, enforced, and so on, in harmony, or conformity, with the domestic law of the signatory. Our domestic law includes RFRA. That would seem to open the door for, in effect, a RFRA exception."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Hollander",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government's position here, that the Court should completely defer to Congress's generalized finding to wholly exempt Schedule 1 of Controlled Substances Act from RFRA's mandate is fundamentally and structurally incompatible with RFRA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But solution is defined by the number of steps in the process that gets the substance into the water? Is that -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Ms. Hollander)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The response to that, Your Honor, is that there is no DMT extracted in this case. Although the Government said that in their brief, there is no evidence of that, and it is contrary to the evidence -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: About commentary or travaux, I don't mind using them for treaties, so long as they don't contradict the Treaty. Do we have any case where we use the -- les travaux preparatoires to actually contradict the language of the Treaty?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Ms. Hollander)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court should do -- even if this Court believes that it's a close question -- should do then what it did in Ashcroft v. ACLU, affirm the preliminary injunction, remand this case for a trial on the merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You think the Treaty gives you a more compelling governmental interest than the Controlled Substances Act?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I certainly do. And the two together, I think, are doubly compelling, because the Government -- the United States has a compelling interest in encouraging this, and section 801(a) -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, not at all. First, the United -- as a general matter, of course, the United States has a compelling interest in living up to its treaties. But, under this Treaty, in particular, the United States has to be in a position to go to other countries, maybe countries that are dragging their feet about whether to take enforcement measures, and say, \"You have an obligation to strictly construe this Convention.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1084",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb1a5773a1db22216b379b46f58aafd5861898d877ed8e52987a154da1b7d6ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb1a5773a1db-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
